  "body": "Native M=1 fetch and integer scalar/pair accesses now execute generated x86 code through the canonical Rust stage-1 walker. The explicit immutable Normal-NC/A=1 profile keeps RAM and table ownership in Rust, adds a separate fixed-width v2 callback ABI, preserves legacy entries, and reports guest faults separately from provider failures. Unsupported controls and attributes stop before architectural commit.\n\nThe change also corrects EL0/EL1 execute permissions, cross-EL cached write permissions, MAIR_EL1 encoding, and impossible callback-fault acknowledgements. Historical BP29 oracle files remain unchanged; active comparisons use a separately named current-source adapter.\n\nValidation: fresh standalone implementation checkout passes package/reference98 tests, actual native C/Rust10 and service39 tests, four semantic negative controls, legacy native/v1/scalar/pair/conditional suites, exact158 Arm comparisons, and UEFI code generation. Independent frozen EFI execution passes108 authored cases plus a wrong-VA-as-PA rejection. Independent service replay preserves354 original architectural matches plus74 BTYPE profile rejections and separately matches78 actual BTYPE=0 ERET fetch cases. The12 QEMU PC-priority deviations remain explicit failures. Final CI-only change requires the already validated UEFI build.\n\nThis bounded profile does not yet provide dynamic control/table changes, normal macOS boot or guest Metal. A trusted callback may commit a store before a malformed acknowledgement is detected; that host-error state is not claimed to be resumable. See docs/NATIVE_MMU_PROVIDER_V2.md.",
